# Where the live co-editing room server lives.
#
# Leave this unset and the app still works completely: the editor, the
# challenges, read aloud, the progress map and offline saving all run on the
# device. What you lose is two people editing the same script at once.
#
# Local development: run `npm run sync` and leave this unset. The app falls
# back to ws://localhost:1234 automatically when it is served from localhost.
#
# Deployed: Vercel cannot host a long-running WebSocket server, so point this
# at one hosted elsewhere (Railway, Render, Fly.io all run
# `npx y-websocket-server` on a free tier). It must be wss://, not ws://, or
# the browser will block it as mixed content.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SYNC_URL=wss://your-sync-host.example.com
